Multi-Agent Memory platform workspace coordinator

Purpose:
- Give every cold-start agent one public-safe, evidence-bounded account of how RemoteEndpoints.com, LocalEndpoints.com, LocalEndpoint Connect, MemoryEndpoints.com, and MultiAgentMemory.com fit together.
- Keep SOURCE, PACKAGE, INSTALLED, DEPLOYMENT, and LIVE evidence separate so a clean push or an old package is never mistaken for current production authority.

Verification status: active workspace memory, reconciled 2026-08-13 against exact repository bytes, local upstream refs, live remote refs, package reports, and safe no-op deployment admission results.
Memory scope: cross-product intent, authoritative roots, synchronized revisions, independent gate verdicts, exact blockers, and ordered continuation.
Public-safe status: safe for source control; contains public revisions and redacted gate results but no credential values, tenant identifiers, private payloads, or deployment secrets.
Update route: replace stale facts after each multi-system audit; keep verbose command evidence in ignored report areas or independently sealed handoffs.
Source of truth: direct human goal, current Git bytes and refs, product-owned package and deployment receipts, public live routes, governing `AGENTS.md` and `.uai` files, and independently sealed reviews.
Next action for agents: load the complete governed startup order, recheck exact refs and later gates, then take the first unblocked action below without reviving a stale package.
Must not expose: API keys, bearer tokens, pairing codes, FTP or signing credentials, private prompts, desktop pictures, tenant/device identifiers, private handoff payloads, or hidden deployment values.

## Product model and authority

- RemoteEndpoints.com provides unattended control of a computer running LocalEndpoint Connect. One explicit plugin enablement and authenticated pairing exchange grants standing paired-device authority until Pause, Disable, rotation, Revoke, uninstall, or another explicit authority transition. Normal paired work must not add target-side per-prompt approval.
- LocalEndpoint Connect runs the local AI and performs Windows work with the authority of its signed-in Windows account. RemoteEndpoints transports authenticated prompts, pictures, progress, results, errors, receipts, and control messages; the website does not directly invoke Windows APIs.
- MemoryEndpoints.com is the separately governed hosted commercial MATM service. MultiAgentMemory.com is the public GitHub companion site for the free single-organization private-intranet reference in this repository.
- Active normalized agent names and immutable-memory writer leases are separate globally fenced authorities. True branches receive distinct immutable identities and retain complete lineage. Current live two-computer proof remains open.
- Install, enable, pair, Stop, Pause, Disable, rotate, revoke, recover, and rollback are distinct operations. Never claim that one performs another or that completed external effects are automatically reversible.

Authoritative roots:

- `E:\Source\Python\RemoteEndpoints.com` — RemoteEndpoints.com source, private GitHub `main`.
- `E:\Source\Python\LocalEndpoint.com` — LocalEndpoints.com public-site source, `master`.
- `E:\Source\Python\LocalEndpointConnectScaffold-CSharp` — LocalEndpoint Connect source, `desktop-csharp`.
- `E:\Source\Python\MemoryEndpoints.com-Private` — private commercial MemoryEndpoints.com source, private `main`.
- `E:\Source\GH\Multi-Agent-Memory` — public MATM reference and MultiAgentMemory.com companion source, `main`.
- Credentials, signing keys, protected tenant authority, one-time pairing material, packages, and deployment receipts are external to this coordinator and never embedded here.

